kind how-do-i
title How do I leave vtium-config after a trial without installing the look yet?
intro When you quit, vtium-config saves your changes into the draft. The console keeps its installed settings until you install the draft.
see install-and-restore/save-on-quit-and-install-from-the-command-line

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type big.
5. Press Enter.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Press Esc.
8. Press t to try live.
9. Press k.
at the kept trial
check console draws mono

10. Press q to quit.
at the quit question
check screen shows "y save and quit"
check screen shows "install"
11. Press y to save and quit.
at the end
check exited 0
check draft look big font-name mono
check installed lacks "big"
# The console draws the font it drew before vtium-config started.
check console draws unifont
